Short Write-up – Titanic Survival Prediction Using Machine Learning
Project Title: First Machine Learning Classifier – Titanic Survival Prediction

Objective: The objective of this project was to build a machine learning classification model to predict whether a passenger survived the Titanic disaster using passenger information.

Dataset and Features: The Titanic dataset (train.csv) was used. Four features were selected: Pclass, Sex, Age, and Fare. The target variable was Survived. Missing values in the Age column were handled using median imputation, and the Sex column was converted into numerical values using Label Encoding.

Model Building: The dataset was divided into training and testing sets using an 80:20 split. A Decision Tree Classifier with a maximum depth of 4 was trained using the Gini criterion.

